stification is sound: E001/E002 → E003 are genuine\n41\tdata/artifact dependencies (the evidence package consolidates the inventories,\n42\tattestations, and test results those epics produce), and the four edges into E005\n43\tare Rule 11 docs-last edges, which do not trigger priority inheritance. Naturally\n44\tparallel work is correctly not serialized: E001 ↔ E002 (different components/repos)\n45\tand E001/E002 ↔ E004 all run parallel, with the E004-to-inventory coupling\n46\texpressed as an acceptance criterion rather than a DAG edge — the rule-compliant\n47\tshape for a consumed reference. Critical path length 3 (E001 → E003 → E005) is\n48\tappropriate for a strategy of this size. Cross-check of epic content found no\n49\tuncaptured data/artifact dependencies.\n50\t\n51\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n52\tE001/E002 are split along the component/team boundary (KServe + data plane under\n53\tRHOAI Serving vs Platform Operator under RHOAI Platform), not by priority. E005\n54\t(docs content) is separated from code work per the work-product rule. No scope\n55\tduplication: E001 and E002 build inventories for disjoint image sets, consolidated\n56\tby E003 — no two epics build the same surface. E001's size overage (all KServe\n57\tcomponent and data plane images in one epic) is handled exactly per the overage\n58\tcarve-out: it is one logical change (a single mechanical remediation pass producing\n59\tone module inventory, where a split would duplicate the audit), and the Health\n60\tWarnings record a concrete, measurable re-split trigger (more than ~3 distinct\n61\timage groups or work spanning multiple owning teams), plus a second trigger for the\n62\tdata-plane ownership ambiguity. A triggered, justified overage does not dock this\n63\tcriterion.\n64\t\n65\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n66\tAll five epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact\n67\t(remediated images + inventory, evidence package, CI gate, published docs). No\n68\tInvestigation epi