rks end to end with FIPS-mode cryptography).\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The module inventory covers every KServe component image and serving data plane image, listing each linked crypto library and its FIPS validation status, and has been reviewed by the owning team.\n45\t- After remediation, no KServe component or serving data plane image links a non-validated crypto library in the request path.\n46\t- Remediated images are verified to run correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: model serving via InferenceService works end to end (deployment reaches Ready, inference requests succeed).\n47\t- All remediated image builds complete successfully in the existing build pipeline after the crypto library changes.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0): All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules — this epic covers the KServe and serving data plane portion.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbfb72a1312524f","agent_id":"aa33c8785972c1ace","session_id":"23bc83d1-dfc9-4a79-8f90-f68a3ba973a8","uuid":"93597605-6872-4d94-b858-20a75f3af015","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:06:16.020Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eb25a3b691bba07","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
