on status, and has been reviewed by the owning team.\n45\t- After remediation, no Platform Operator image links a non-validated crypto library.\n46\t- The remediated operator is verified to run correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster: it installs and reconciles the model serving stack (custom resources reach their Ready conditions).\n47\t- All remediated image builds complete successfully in the existing build pipeline after the crypto library changes.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0): All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules — this epic covers the Platform Operator portion.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbfb72a1312524f","agent_id":"aa33c8785972c1ace","session_id":"23bc83d1-dfc9-4a79-8f90-f68a3ba973a8","uuid":"2d7a5a58-e04e-433a-9803-beef93ce02ff","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:06:16.666Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac52654648f3e520","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
