idence package contains the module inventory, build attestations, and test results for every serving-stack image in scope (KServe components, serving data plane, Platform Operator), with no gaps against the consolidated inventories.\n47\t- The evidence package passes the security review board review at the defined milestones and is accepted for submission.\n48\t- The evidence package is submitted to the external accredited certification laboratory.\n49\t\n50\t## Risks / Notes\n51\t\n52\t- Certification laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months and the review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They are schedule risks, not conditions this epic's deliverable produces.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-2 (P0): A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbfb72a1312524f","agent_id":"aa33c8785972c1ace","session_id":"23bc83d1-dfc9-4a79-8f90-f68a3ba973a8","uuid":"bce23e72-f523-4e43-95ff-0ac30894f019","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:06:17.160Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a6c894a2178a75b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
